{
	"Name": "OKTA_RISK_SCORE",
	"Description": "Scores an enriched Okta System Log event from 0-100 and buckets it into a priority. Expand the macro in the search GUI to read every scoring rule inline; nothing is hidden behind further macros.\n\nRequires these enumerated values to exist before the macro runs:\n  - eventType, severity, outcomeResult, isProxy (from the json module)\n  - category, subcategory, is_mod (from: lookup -r okta_eventTypes)\n  - actor_weight (from: lookup -r okta_privileged_actor)\n  - target_weight (from: lookup -r okta_protected_target)\n  - actorUserNorm, targetUserNorm (lower-cased usernames, used as the heuristic fallback)\n\nProduces:\n  - risk_score: 0-100 integer\n  - _priority: Informational | Low | Medium | High | Critical\n  - is_mod_final: 1 when the event changed configuration, else 0\n\nScoring, in six commented steps:\n  1. Base score from the event type. Signing keys and OAuth2 client changes score 85-90, sign-on policy and credential/factor resets 80, network zones 75, app and group grants 70, device enrollment 65, hooks and IdP changes 60, org settings and security events 55, everything else 35.\n  2. Flag configuration changes using okta_eventTypes is_mod, falling back to the verb on the end of the event type.\n  3. Modification bump: +15 when the base is under 60, +8 when under 80.\n  4. Signal bumps: severity ERROR +10 / WARN +5, successful outcome +5, anonymising proxy +5.\n  5. Account sensitivity: explicit lookup weight, else +8 for privileged actors and +12 for protected targets matched by name.\n  6. Total, clamp to 0-100, bucket: Critical \u003e= 90, High \u003e= 75, Medium \u003e= 55, Low \u003e= 35, else Informational.\n\nUsage:\ntag=$OKTA\n| json eventType severity outcome.result as outcomeResult securityContext.isProxy as isProxy\n| lookup -r okta_eventTypes eventType eventType (category subcategory is_mod)\n$OKTA_RISK_SCORE\n\nReference(s):\n  - https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n  - https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	]
}